{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Python 3 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Python 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport sys\nimport itertools\n\nn = int(sys.stdin.readline().strip())\n\ninputA = list(map(int, sys.stdin.readline().strip().split()))\ninputB = list(map(int, sys.stdin.readline().strip().split()))\n\ninputA2 = [x for x in inputA]\ninputB2 = [x for x in inputB]\n\n\ndef getWonMaxFast(a, b):\n    wins = [0, 0, 0]\n    for i in range(3):\n        j = (i + 1) % 3\n        match_count = min(a[i], b[j])\n        wins[i] = match_count\n        a[i] -= match_count\n        b[j] -= match_count\n    return sum(wins)\n\n\ndef getLostMaxFast(a, b):\n    patterns = [[0, 2], [1, 0], [2, 1], [0, 0], [1, 1], [2, 2]]\n    max_loss = 0\n    \n    for perm in itertools.permutations(patterns):\n        losses = [0, 0, 0]\n        temp_a = a.copy()\n        temp_b = b.copy()\n        \n        for src_idx, dst_idx in perm:\n            transfer = min(temp_a[src_idx], temp_b[dst_idx])\n            temp_a[src_idx] -= transfer\n            temp_b[dst_idx] -= transfer\n            losses[src_idx] += transfer\n        \n        total = sum(losses)\n        if total > max_loss:\n            max_loss = total\n    \n    return max_loss\n\n\nlost = getLostMaxFast(inputA2, inputB2)\nwon = getWonMaxFast(inputA, inputB)\nprint(n - lost, won)\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);\n        \n        int n = Integer.parseInt(scanner.nextLine().trim());\n        \n        String[] line1 = scanner.nextLine().trim().split(\"\\\\s+\");\n        String[] line2 = scanner.nextLine().trim().split(\"\\\\s+\");\n        \n        int[] inputA = new int[3];\n        int[] inputB = new int[3];\n        \n        for (int i = 0; i < 3; i++) {\n            inputA[i] = Integer.parseInt(line1[i]);\n            inputB[i] = Integer.parseInt(line2[i]);\n        }\n        \n        int[] inputA2 = Arrays.copyOf(inputA, inputA.length);\n        int[] inputB2 = Arrays.copyOf(inputB, inputB.length);\n        \n        int lost = getLostMaxFast(inputA2, inputB2);\n        int won = getWonMaxFast(inputA, inputB);\n        \n        System.out.println((n - lost) + \" \" + won);\n    }\n    \n    private static int getWonMaxFast(int[] a, int[] b) {\n        int[] wins = new int[3];\n        for (int i = 0; i < 3; i++) {\n            int j = (i + 1) % 3;\n            int matchCount = Math.min(a[i], b[j]);\n            wins[i] = matchCount;\n            a[i] -= matchCount;\n            b[j] -= matchCount;\n        }\n        return wins[0] + wins[1] + wins[2];\n    }\n    \n    private static int getLostMaxFast(int[] a, int[] b) {\n        int[][] patterns = {\n            {0, 2},\n            {1, 0},\n            {2, 1},\n            {0, 0},\n            {1, 1},\n            {2, 2}\n        };\n        \n        int maxLoss = 0;\n        \n        // Generate all permutations of patterns\n        int[][] allPermutations = generatePermutations(patterns);\n        \n        for (int[][] perm : allPermutations) {\n            int[] losses = new int[3];\n            int[] tempA = Arrays.copyOf(a, a.length);\n            int[] tempB = Arrays.copyOf(b, b.length);\n            \n            for (int[] pair : perm) {\n                int srcIdx = pair[0];\n                int dstIdx = pair[1];\n                int transfer = Math.min(tempA[srcIdx], tempB[dstIdx]);\n                tempA[srcIdx] -= transfer;\n                tempB[dstIdx] -= transfer;\n                losses[srcIdx] += transfer;\n            }\n            \n            int total = losses[0] + losses[1] + losses[2];\n            if (total > maxLoss) {\n                maxLoss = total;\n            }\n        }\n        \n        return maxLoss;\n    }\n    \n    private static int[][][] generatePermutations(int[][] array) {\n        List<int[][]> result = new ArrayList<>();\n        permute(array, 0, result);\n        return result.toArray(new int[0][][]);\n    }\n    \n    private static void permute(int[][] array, int start, List<int[][]> result) {\n        if (start == array.length) {\n            // Create a deep copy of the current permutation\n            int[][] copy = new int[array.length][2];\n            for (int i = 0; i < array.length; i++) {\n                copy[i][0] = array[i][0];\n                copy[i][1] = array[i][1];\n            }\n            result.add(copy);\n            return;\n        }\n        \n        for (int i = start; i < array.length; i++) {\n            swap(array, start, i);\n            permute(array, start + 1, result);\n            swap(array, start, i);\n        }\n    }\n    \n    private static void swap(int[][] array, int i, int j) {\n        int[] temp = array[i];\n        array[i] = array[j];\n        array[j] = temp;\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00015722469834145159, -1.9073468138230965e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -2.586808113846928e-05, -5.2689116